From 1d53d3a249089df342406af74fa465240abe4791 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redgrave961 <214504937+Redgrave961@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:17:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SPU: one approximate single-precision path; cheaper DMA
 overlay check and MFC calls

- fa/fs/fm/fma/fms/fnms are the host op in the SPU's mode (round toward zero,
  denormals as zero, set by spu_run_with_halt), saturated to +-Smax with any
  zero made +0. The exact extended-range forms, their slow paths, the per-run
  mode flag and the exact float tests are removed; the lifter emits plain calls
- spu_overlay_note_get prefetches every candidate region's source line before
  comparing, so the misses overlap
- mfc_claim stays out of line so mfc_for inlines; mfc_channel_read drops the
  engine argument it never used
- The reservation notify loads a holder's resv before its compare-and-swap
